TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains a second time with nothing in the lane to own: HEAD is still 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all --ignored` is empty, the task diff is empty, and neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh nor any new file under tests/ exists on disk. The 10 s finalMessage projection timeout (result-projection-timeout, exitEvidencePassed=false) is the same downstream symptom recorded on attempt 1, not an independent machinery fault, so this is not transient. Attempt 1 was already diagnosed retry with maximally explicit steering that spelled out the terminal sequence (run the acceptance argv, git add only in-domain paths, git commit, confirm a clean status); attempt 2 reproduced the identical zero-commit outcome, which exhausts the hard two-attempt cap and removes retry as an available verdict. Two out-of-task facts also block a clean repeat of the task as currently written: (1) authorized-comment 7 directs the worker to `git add` results/receipts/proxy.json, but results/ is not in this task's conflictDomains [\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\"], so obeying the authoritative steering is precisely what the conflict-domains gate rejects, while disobeying it leaves the receipt the campaign expects untracked — the operator must resolve that contradiction by either granting results/receipts/proxy.json or amending the steering; (2) authorized-comment 7 also asserts that the proxy checkpoint at /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy survives from prior attempts, but that path does not exist on this host, so any future attempt must budget for building the checkpoint from scratch inside the container rather than reusing it. Substantive engine findings from steering remain valid and should carry forward unchanged: serve text-only with --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0,\"video\":0}' to avoid the vision-encoder profiling allocation, keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6, do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY=0 (superseded, integrated_gpu=False on this host), and optionally export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True. The decisive ordering lesson is that the acceptance criterion is only `bash -n` plus a grep for the literal receipt path, so the two scripts can and must be authored and committed before any container build or GPU serve is attempted; both attempts appear to have spent the session on the heavy runtime path and ended before the commit that ownership validates.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/make-proxy.sh","scripts/run-proxy.sh","tests","results/receipts/proxy.json"],"goal":"Re-issue the proxy-tooling work with results/receipts/proxy.json added to the write boundary and with a commit-first ordering that decouples authoring the scripts from exercising them on the GPU. Deliverable 1 (must land as a commit before any container or GPU work begins): scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh written in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh (bash shebang, set -euo pipefail, REPO_ROOT derived from dirname, IMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\", podman run with --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host and -v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\", heredoc'd python payload), per specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4 and the cited evidence notes. make-proxy.sh runs inside the container and synthesizes a tiny checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's own tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout rather than inventing a generator, and it must not assume /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy already exists because it does not. run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1, eager execution, gpu_memory_utilization 0.6, and --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0,\"video\":0}' (text-only mode, which is what avoids the 274877906944-byte vision-encoder profiling allocation), requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits through the API, shuts down cleanly, writes results/receipts/proxy.json, and records the text-only flag choice in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. Deliverable 2 (separate commit, after the first has landed): the receipt produced by an actual run, now inside the boundary. The worker must finish every attempt with a clean `git status --porcelain`.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"proxy-scripts-clean","description":"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.","argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh"]},{"id":"proxy-scripts-committed","description":"Both scripts are tracked at HEAD and the worktree is clean, which is the condition attempts 1 and 2 failed.","argv":["bash","-euc","git ls-files --error-unmatch scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh >/dev/null && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\""]},{"id":"proxy-serve-flags-recorded","description":"run-proxy.sh encodes the established serve doctrine so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it: PLE mmap on, eager execution, and text-only multimodal limits.","argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qi 'enforce.eager\\|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh"]},{"id":"proxy-no-out-of-domain-paths","description":"Every path touched by the task commits stays inside the amended boundary, including the receipt.","argv":["bash","-euc","git diff --name-only 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa..HEAD | grep -vE '^(scripts/make-proxy\\.sh|scripts/run-proxy\\.sh|tests/|results/receipts/proxy\\.json$)' | { ! grep -q .; }"]}],"dependencies":[]}}
